/*	This original unicode glyph scheme for sprite names is a simplified name-desc with game/filesystem accepted
	  characters. Each decor group [asset]/*.png for better asset mgmt and editor UI naming.
	Characters render 🗹 in-game, 🗹 explorer.exe (win10), 🗹 excel (2016), 🗹 notepad, but not 🗵 cmd.exe
	  or 🗵 powershell [5] (however they will copy from cmd correctly despite not font rendering in cmd).
	These symbols were 𝑚𝑒𝑡𝑖𝑐𝑢𝑙𝑜𝑢𝑠𝑙𝑦 selected for clarity and relativity, reducing long names to a few
	  readable glyphs. Consideration given towards in-game panel info box clarity.

	In our hex-squares, we use up⮝/down⮟ prefixes. To achieve the hex-square effect, high/low assets horizontally
	  link to their opposing vertical adjacency (i.e. high path is seamless to low path).

	High or low glyph context: ⮝ ⮟
		Rivers/paths: ║ ˭ ‗ ╝ ╚ ╔ ╗ ╦ ╩ ╣ ╠
		River endpoints: ⩓ ⩔ ⋖ ⋗
		Beaches: ◢ ◥ ◤ ◣
		Shores: ◸ ◹ ◺ ◿
		Non-decor left/right space: ▀ ▄

	Did an experiment mapping out parts of the original Britannia with Excel. Noting here for now, unused atm:
		Grassland,Flatland,Desert,Mountain: ■ ▥ ▤ ▣
		Coast, Surf, Ocean: ▨ ▧ ⬜
		Scrub/Woods/Forest/Thicket: ▵ △ ▲ ◆
		Swamp,Hill,River: ▩ ▦ ═
*/

